depending on who you ask Marvel's  nocturnal hero moon night is either a  mercenary an emissary of an ancient  Egyptian god an obvious Batman clone or  just an absolute lunatic over the years  countless revivals and reinterpretations  have given readers reason to think of  them in any of those ways and more as a  side effect moon nights origins and even  the core of his character can be tough  to figure out asking a question as  simple as what's moon nights secret  identity is complicated enough to make  you shake your head so to help you along  here's the truth about moon night moon  nights real-life namesake rather than  the usual hero everyman dichotomy were  used to with Superman and Clark Kent or  spider-man and Peter Parker Boone Knight  has at least three civilian names fairs  taxi driver Jake Lockley the mercenary  marc spector and millionaire stephen  graham these three identities not only  speak and act differently the people in  moon knights life choose who they  believe is the dominant persona his  girlfriend marlene for instance only  ever refers to him as Steven whether or  not he's wearing the mask co-creator  Doug much on the other hand cast moon  Knights dominant persona as Mark Specter  a name he got from an employee at a  comic shop that Monch called the best  comic shop in Manhattan at the time he  often used the names of people in his  life for new characters and as he says  one of the guys who worked there was  Mark Specter when the employee asked  when are you gonna name a comic-book  character after me Maj decided to use  his name for a new villain he was  creating for an issue of werewolf by  night with that moon Knights got a name  and the real-life mark Spectre got his  wish moon Knights villainous roots March  and artist Don Perlin first brought Moon  Knight to life in 1975 s werewolf by  night number 32 as a mercenary hired by  a clandestine group known only as the  committee to capture a werewolf named  Jack Russell now really like the 