us as a Holocaust survivor wouldn't  be revealed until 1981 similarly doc  Samson's Jewish heritage wasn't  discussed until 1990 well after the  character's debut in the pages of  Incredible Hulk so whether or not he was  the first Moon Knight was the first one  whose heritage was discussed on the page  either way it's a milestone the Hawkeye  connection Moon Knight has never been  much of a team player but in the late  80s his status as an up-and-coming fan  favorite character  landed him a spot on the West Coast  Avengers and gave them a pretty  interesting source for his  crime-fighting equipment in 1987 West  Coast Avengers number 23 the LA based  team went back in time to ancient Egypt  once there they found worshippers of the  Moon God  kunchu the patron deity who brought bark  Spectre back from the dead and charged  him to fight for justice under siege  determined to help the Egyptians defend  themselves hawkeye designed weapons for  them like darts and boomerangs the issue  ends with a cut back to modern times  where we see mark Specter finding the  same weapons his fellow Avenger design  to date we don't know if moon night or  [ __ ] you have offered Hawkeye royalties  or even just a co-creator credit if not  maybe Clint Barton should think about  retaining the services of Nelson and  Murdock for the inevitable litigation  movie night plans for an adaptation of  Moon Knight have seemed to be in the  works for years mostly on the small  screen the name mark Specter was  mentioned on an episode of the  short-lived Blade television series in  which sticky fingers from the rap group  onyx took over for Wesley Snipes  subsequently Marvel Studios partnered  with no equal entertainment to develop a  show based on the hero and once Netflix  launched their defenders series rumors  started swirling that the fist of  khonshu would fit right in with the  street-level side of the Marvel Universe  even recent Moon Knight comics have  provided an episodic psychological  t